{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1488735549,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMTE5Njg5MzY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1357","origin":"github"},"title":"using Control socket logging into systems using kerberos/afs does not gain necessary permissions/variables","message":"it might as well be the problem specific to our system setup (will clarify with the admin) but was worth reporting imho.\n\nIf I first establish the ssh socket first (and login/permissions work just nice in there), the subsequent calls to ssh do not gain needed permissions to access $HOME and also does not get correct $PATH settings... so feels like then it does not process \"login\" settings for the shell (i.e. /etc/profile etc), even if a session is interactive:\n```shell\n$\u003e ssh -o 'ControlPath=/home/yoh/.cache/datalad/sockets/258a056af1cad68ee3e93a7012d80a88' yohtest@rolando.cns            \nCould not chdir to home directory /afs/dbic.dartmouth.edu/usr/haxby/yohtest: Permission denied\n-bash: /afs/dbic.dartmouth.edu/usr/haxby/yohtest/.bash_profile: Permission denied\n```\n\nthat causes all kinds of troubles when trying to `datalad install` from that system, requiring more than a single 'ssh' interaction (e.g. `datalad install -r`)","files":null}]}